<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>God is incarnate in the flesh that we</l><l>Him may receive, experience ourself;</l><l>This is the grace which we receive of God,</l><l>Which comes thru Christ and which is Christ Himself.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Paul the Apostle counted all as dung,</l><l>’Twas only God in Christ he counted grace;</l><l>’Tis by this grace—the Lord experienced—</l><l>That he surpassed the others in the race.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>It is this grace—Christ as our inward strength—</l><l>Which with His all-sufficiency doth fill;</l><l>It is this grace which in our spirit is,</l><l>There energizing, working out God’s will.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>This grace, which is the living Christ Himself,</l><l>Is what we need and must experience;</l><l>Lord, may we know this grace and by it live,</l><l>Thyself increasingly as grace to sense.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
